Shelley:  please file this information for development into a website topic=
 for product and use & installation instructions.

All,

There are two items in the PE price sheet that are used when forces in a pi=
peline need to be transferred "out of the pipeline".  The Thrust Anchor app=
ears in the Transition Fittings and Adapters section.  The Flex Restraint, =
an electrofusion component, appears in the Electrofusion section.  The Thru=
st Anchor is also referred to as a Wall Anchor.

Thrust Anchor/Wall Anchor
[cid:image001.png@01D1E655.4796F860]

Flex Restraint
[cid:image002.png@01D1E655.4796F860]

Note below their depictions in their application excerpted from chapter 7 o=
f the PE Handbook on the Plastic Pipe Institute website at www.plasticpipe.=
org<http://www.plasticpipe.org>.

[cid:image009.png@01D1E655.4796F860]
They are both encased in a designed concrete structure that transfers the t=
hrust to the surrounding soil or to some other structure.  This is a nontri=
vial design effort that is outside the scope of Harco's "supply".  Users sh=
ould start with the PE Handbook and the Field Manual for Municipal Water Ap=
plications which can be found on the Plastic Pipe Institute website at www.=
plasticpipe.org<http://www.plasticpipe.org>.  The services of a professiona=
l engineer experienced in such applications may be required.

The Flex Restraint installation instructions are attached.  Also attached i=
s a chart for pipe diameters up to 48" that describes how many restraints e=
qually spaced about the circumference are required to develop the full thru=
st of a given DR at its rated pressure.  It may be used on diameters from 6=
" to 48".  This chart will be included in the price sheet.

Note that as one goes up in diameter and down in DR one is limited by the n=
umber of these that can be installed about a diameter.  This means the thru=
st transfer capability is limited to that of a higher DR in that size.  We =
cannot recommend adding flex restraints up or down stream through another c=
ross section to increase this thrust transfer capability.

J

